FFmpeg — GNU General Public License

  Bundled as a per-platform static sidecar (src-tauri/binaries/ffmpeg-<triple>),
  fetched and checksum-pinned by scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.sh. Neither build is
  configured with --enable-nonfree, which would make it unredistributable.

  Note the two platforms ship under DIFFERENT versions of the GPL, so both
  licence texts are included:

  macOS (aarch64-apple-darwin) — FFmpeg 8.1, GPL-2.0-or-later
    See LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt
    --enable-gpl --enable-libx264 --enable-libx265 --enable-libvpx
    --enable-libaom --enable-libsvtav1 --enable-libvvenc --enable-libkvazaar
    --enable-libopus --enable-libmp3lame --enable-libvorbis --enable-libtheora
    --enable-libopenjpeg --enable-libwebp --enable-libass --enable-libfreetype
    --enable-fontconfig --enable-libharfbuzz --enable-libvmaf --enable-libzimg
    --enable-libvidstab --enable-libsnappy --enable-neon
    --enable-runtime-cpudetect --pkg-config-flags=--static

  Windows (x86_64-pc-windows-msvc) — FFmpeg n8.1, GPL-3.0-or-later
    See LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt
    --enable-gpl --enable-version3 --disable-libfdk-aac --enable-libx264
    --enable-libfreetype --enable-libharfbuzz --enable-libfribidi
    --enable-fontconfig --enable-ffnvcodec --enable-libvpl --enable-amf

  libfreetype is not optional: without it FFmpeg has no drawtext filter and
  burned-in captions silently do not render. Homebrew's own build lacks it,
  which is why the fetch script gates on its presence.

  WRITTEN OFFER: the complete corresponding source for these FFmpeg builds is
  available from https://ffmpeg.org/download.html at the tagged version above,
  and on request from the address in the repository README.

  ⚖️ PRE-LAUNCH: the macOS build is currently sourced from osxexperts.net,
  which labels its downloads "for educational purposes only". That wording is
  incompatible with redistribution and must be resolved — by building FFmpeg
  ourselves or sourcing from a vendor with clear redistribution terms — before
  any public release.
